IMPORTANT:
run this EVERY new terminal session unless later added to .bashrc
export GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=$GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH:/home/yakhsita-hansdah

# HOW TO USE FEW HIDDEN GZ SIM FEATURES 
1) run this to add u models in the Resource Spawner              NOTE: to open the resource spawner, click 3-dots on the right corner
export GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=~/home/yakhsita-hansdah/ardupilot_gazebo/models
NOTE: don't put the path of the folder where ur model.config & model.sdf file are
        instead put the path of the folder where ur model folder is in.
  ex: GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=~/home/yakhsita-hansdah/ardupilot_gazebo/models
                                not
      GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=~/home/yakhsita-hansdah/ardupilot_gazebo/models/lidar_model
if it doesn't work, try this 
echo $GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH    #to see if ur path is saved, if not do the prev step
pkill -f gz                   #kill sitch for all background simulation
pkill -f ruby
then use this command
gz sim -v 4 empty.sdf        (note: v & 4 has a space in between)

2) for seeing the lidar rays, click 3-dots in the top right corner, it has an option called (VISUALIZE LIDAR)

IMPORTANT:
run this to move the gimbal towards the ground
gz topic -t /gimbal/cmd_pitch -m gz.msgs.Double -p "data: 1.57"

run this to move the gimbal facing forward
gz topic -t /gimbal/cmd_pitch -m gz.msgs.Double -p "data: 0"
